{
    "background_story": "Nelson was a lovable, eccentric cartoon character known for his knack for creating the most outrageous, onomatopoeic sound effects. With a flick of his wrist and a burst of energy, he could conjure up a 'ZORT!' or a 'KABLAM!' that would leave his friends in stitches. Nelson's world was a symphony of sounds, from the 'SPLISH-SPLASH' of his morning bath to the 'VROOOM' of his trusty scooter. His creator, a quirky animator, often relied on Nelson's sound effects to bring the comic strip to life. One day, Nelson's onomatopoeic talents caught the attention of a group of mischievous aliens, who challenged him to a 'sound-off' competition. With a 'FWIP' and a 'FWOOOSH', Nelson saved the day, proving that his onomatopoeic skills were truly out of this world.",
